  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Beans on toast is tinned baked beans heated on the hob and spooned over thick buttered toast. The version most people eat is worse than it needs to be: beans poured cold from the tin over pale unbuttered bread. Done properly, with real butter on hot toast and a little seasoning stirred into the beans, it is a proper quick meal."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 2,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "baked-beans",
              "amount": 800,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "two 400 g tins",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "bread-white",
              "amount": 4,
              "unit": "each",
              "prepNote": "thick-cut slices",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "salted-butter",
              "amount": 30,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "worcestershire-sauce",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": true,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "black-pepper",
              "amount": null,
              "unit": "grind",
              "prepNote": "to taste",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A small saucepan and a toaster are all you need."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Warm the beans"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Tip {{baked-beans}} of baked beans into a small saucepan over medium heat. Add a dash of {{worcestershire-sauce}} of Worcestershire sauce and a good pinch of black pepper."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stir occasionally for 3 to 4 minutes until hot throughout. Remove from the heat and stir in a small knob of the {{salted-butter}} of butter."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Toast and assemble"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Toast the {{bread-white}} slices until golden. Butter generously with the remaining {{salted-butter}} of butter while the toast is still hot."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pile the beans on top and serve at once."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "rows": [
            {
              "symptom": "Beans are watery",
              "cause": "Too much sauce in the tin and heat too low to reduce it",
              "fix": "Raise the heat slightly and stir more often. The sauce will thicken as it heats."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Toast goes soggy",
              "cause": "Beans poured over before the butter had a chance to soak in",
              "fix": "Butter the toast first and leave it for 30 seconds before adding the beans."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Beans taste flat",
              "cause": "No seasoning added during heating",
              "fix": "Add black pepper and a small dash of Worcestershire sauce while the beans heat. A knob of butter stirred in at the end lifts the flavour."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Toast is pale and soft under the beans",
              "cause": "Not toasted long enough",
              "fix": "Toast until clearly golden on both sides. Pale toast goes limp once the beans hit it."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Variations"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Beans on toast with cheese: grate a generous amount of cheddar over the beans on the toast and place under a hot grill for two minutes until bubbling. Beans with a poached egg on top adds protein for a more filling meal."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Baked beans arrived in Britain from America in the early twentieth century. By the post-war decades, beans on toast was one of the most common quick meals in the country. It sits alongside scrambled eggs on toast and cheese on toast in the British repertoire. It is fast, filling, and known by almost everyone."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
